WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:06.025
Lab 1 runs in the provider notices
folder of the examples, in PowerShell 7.

3
00:00:06.025 --> 00:00:08.800
The teams in the lab's
routing are fictional.

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.763
Step one checks the lab's routing:
seven rules, in the order they're tried.

5
00:00:13.763 --> 00:00:19.404
Six route to a task: security operations
at P2, cloud platform engineering

6
00:00:19.404 --> 00:00:24.399
at P3 twice, the service desk at P2
twice, and cloud operations at P3.

7
00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:26.000
The seventh ignores.

8
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.486
Rule R04b makes every open Microsoft
365 incident a task: Microsoft 365

9
00:00:32.486 --> 00:00:39.412
service health names no resources, so
R04, which needs them, never matches one.

10
00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:41.798
Step two tries the template as it ships,

11
00:00:41.798 --> 00:00:45.301
and the kit refuses it, because
it still has a placeholder.

12
00:00:45.301 --> 00:00:49.238
It runs only once every
value is filled in, at work.

13
00:00:49.238 --> 00:00:53.479
Step three collects every provider
from the day-one fixtures:

14
00:00:53.479 --> 00:00:55.724
twenty-two notices, as in Module 1.

15
00:00:55.724 --> 00:00:58.187
Step four routes them as a dry run.

16
00:00:58.187 --> 00:00:59.926
Twenty-two new notices.

17
00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:04.314
Thirteen route to a task,
eight go to the digest only,

18
00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:08.913
and one is ignored: the
Microsoft Viva post, by rule R06.

19
00:01:08.913 --> 00:01:15.425
The open Exchange Online incident is a
P2 task for the service desk, by R04b.

20
00:01:15.425 --> 00:01:20.020
That's thirteen create payloads,
written to a folder, and nothing sent.
